    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "We’ve all had cuts and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "scrapes",
            "zh": "割伤与擦伤"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But how do we "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "heal",
            "ref": "v-heal"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "? In many cases, the process requires the forming of a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "scab",
            "zh": "痂"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Scabs aren’t much fun to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "deal with",
            "ref": "v-deal-with"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Still, they’re an important part of the healing process."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Scabs always start with "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "injuries",
            "ref": "v-injury"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to the skin. When your body realizes it’s been injured, it will form a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "blood clot",
            "zh": "血凝块"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The clot helps to stop the bleeding from your "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "wound",
            "ref": "v-wound"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". That’s when your injury starts to heal. As your skin "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "tissues",
            "ref": "v-tissue"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " grow, they push the blood clot outward. That’s how it ends up as a scab over your wound. It helps protect you from "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "infection",
            "ref": "v-infection"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " by keeping "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "germs",
            "zh": "病菌"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " out of your wound."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Scabs can be "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "itchy",
            "ref": "v-itchy"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". They are often uncomfortable, but it’s important to let them do their job. Picking at a scab can lead to infection and other problems."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "There are also a few ways you can help your scabs to heal. For example, it helps to keep the area clean by washing it with soap and water. It can also help to use "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "bandages",
            "ref": "v-bandage"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to protect the scab."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
